@talks work:watch
// TW1, the Talk a while work pools: Watch (plans/work-pools-plan.html, decided 2026-10-20). Rounds, doors, airlocks,
// the Watch office, "friendly on patrol, firm at the airlock". Ids work.watch.<slug>; topic always "work".
// Holt has his own talks (doors, rounds) and skips nearly all of these; never his suit-locker test (beat 1). Tomas:
// never the exam or the transfer list. Exams theme (Nakamura, Castellano): no exam or study talk.
// Night Watch: mensah achterberg-lars garcia-greta park-noor castellano-jem. Cadet: dufresne-cora.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- acquaintance: the job up close

== door-sounds
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:holt
them: A good door goes "tunk". A tired one goes "tank". I know them by sound now.
them: I report the tanks. Then someone from Works turns up with a spanner.   #funny
ask: Is there a sound on this ship you'd know anywhere?
listen: What happens to the tired doors?
  them: Works gets a note. Then someone like you fixes it. That's the circle.   #warm
share: The lift chime. It means nearly home.
  them: Good one. That's on my list too.
cheer: The kettle at the tea corner.
  them: So's the whole ship. It boils, we come.   #funny

== lift-view
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:holt|tomas
them: From the Watch office you see the lift all day. Tomas says it's the best view aboard.
them: He's not wrong. You learn who's late, who's early, who holds the lift for others.   #warm
ask: What do you notice first about someone new?
listen: Who's always late?
  them: I couldn't possibly say. Torres. Breakfast. Every day. Ten more minutes with the coils.   #funny
share: Whether they say hello first.
  them: Good test. The Wren passes it, mostly. You did, first day.   #warm
cheer: Their shoes. Very telling.
  them: Ha. Works boots are the worst. Sorry. Correct, though.   #funny

== firm-airlock
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:holt
them: Friendly on patrol, firm at the airlock. That's the Watch in one line.
them: You can be anyone's friend in a corridor. At an airlock, you check every seal. Twice.
ask: Is there a place where you're stricter than usual?
listen: Has anyone ever argued at an airlock?
  them: Once. Then they saw my face. It's a very patient face. They stopped.   #funny
share: My toolkit. Nobody borrows it unasked.
  them: Good. Everyone needs one airlock. Yours is a toolbox.   #funny
cheer: My bunk ladder. Nobody climbs it.
  them: That's not an airlock. That's a border. Fair, though.   #funny

== rounds-walk
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:holt
them: A round's every deck, end to end. You learn the ship with your feet.
them: I could find my way blindfold now. I'm not allowed to try. I've asked.   #funny
ask: Do you know the ship by heart yet, or still learning?
listen: How long does a full round take?
  them: An hour if it's quiet. Two if people want to chat. They always want to chat.   #warm
share: Still learning. Deck 2 beats me every time.
  them: Deck 2 beats everyone. The corridor's a loop. It's a trick.   #funny
cheer: By smell. Three's toast, five's oil.
  them: That's a real Watch skill. Don't laugh. I mean it.   #funny

== night-rounds
when: tier>=acquaintance who:mensah|achterberg-lars|garcia-greta|park-noor|castellano-jem
them: Night rounds, the lights are low and every door's shut. You hear the ship breathing.
them: Somebody always leaves a cup in the mess. I wash it. Nobody knows. That's the job too.   #warm
ask: What would you hear, if you walked the ship at night?
listen: Is it ever spooky?
  them: Only the garden. The leaves rustle in the fans. Gets me every time.   #funny
share: The hum. And my own footsteps.
  them: That's it exactly. Mind you, the hum gets louder at three. I've noticed.
cheer: Someone snoring through a wall.
  them: Someone in Bunk 2 talks about engines in their sleep. I've stopped logging it.   #funny

== log-book
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:holt
them: Everything goes in the Watch log. Doors, lamps, who came back late. Neat as you like.
them: Calm in a crisis, fussy about paperwork. That's what they say about us. Fair.   #funny
ask: Do you keep any kind of log? Notes, a diary, lists?
listen: What's the oddest thing in the log?
  them: "02:14. Cactus in the corridor. Returned to owner. Owner asleep." It was a Gerald.   #funny
share: A few notes on my device. Mostly jobs.
  them: Good. Notes are a kindness to tomorrow's you. Tomorrow's you is grateful.
cheer: Only a list of who owes me a favour.
  them: That's a log. A very important log. Keep it current.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- colleague: why this job

== why-watch
when: tier>=colleague !who:holt|tomas|dufresne-cora !thread:stuck|leaving|startover
them: I picked the Watch because I like knowing everyone's all right. That's all it is, really.
them: Some people count stars. I count heads. Seventy-five, every shift. All present.   #warm
ask: What made you pick the job you do? The real reason.
listen: What if a head's missing?
  them: Then I find them. Usually asleep in the observatory. Once, the garden.   #funny
share: I like fixing things. Simple as that.
  them: Not so different. We both make sure the ship's all right. Different spanners.   #warm
cheer: The orange was taken. Works got it.
  them: Ours is very dignified. You'd look awful in it.   #funny

== holt-lectures
when: tier>=colleague !who:holt|mensah|tomas|dufresne-cora|castellano-jem
them: I learnt the Watch from Holt. One lecture at a time. There were a lot of lectures.
them: "Name every door between here and the mess." Every day. For a month.   #funny
ask: Who's the strictest teacher you've ever had?
listen: Was it worth it?
  them: Every word. I'd find you in the dark on any deck. That's Holt, in me.   #warm
share: Someone at home. Hard, but fair.
  them: Those are the ones you end up thanking. Years later. Silently.   #warm
cheer: A very stern swimming teacher.
  them: Ha. Holt would make an excellent swimming teacher. Terrifying, but nobody sinks.   #funny

== airlock-check
when: tier>=colleague !who:holt
them: Seal check takes four minutes. I do it in four minutes. Never three.
them: The day you do it in three is the day you miss something. I've never missed something.
ask: What's the thing you never rush, however busy you are?
listen: Has a seal ever failed a check?
  them: Twice. Little things. Works came. Nobody was near it. That's the point of four minutes.
share: Anything live. I always isolate first.
  them: Good. Same idea. Rush the tea, not the seal.
cheer: Breakfast. I savour it.
  them: That's allowed. Breakfast's a kind of safety check too.   #funny

== people-not-doors
when: tier>=colleague !who:holt|mensah
them: The best Watch tool isn't a scanner. It's a cup of tea, offered at the right door.
them: Half our rounds end with a chat. Holt calls it "patrolling". We don't argue.   #funny
ask: Who looks out for the people who look out for everyone?
listen: Do people mind being noticed?
  them: Some do. So we're subtle. A cup left outside a door is very subtle.   #funny
share: Each other. That's how it should work.
  them: That's exactly how it works. On a good ship. This is a good ship.   #warm
cheer: The Captain. She notices everything.
  them: She does. Don't tell her we know. She likes to think it's a secret.   #funny

== parent-served
when: tier>=colleague who:dahl-mira|shah-dara
them: My parent served on the Wren, years ago. I found the name in an old crew list.
them: Two others aboard have the same story. We look at the portrait gallery and wonder.   #warm
ask: Is there anyone in your family who did a job like yours?
listen: Did they serve together, do you think?
  them: Maybe. Nobody's checked. It's nicer not knowing, a bit. More possible.   #warm
share: Not really. I'm the first.
  them: Then you're starting something. Somebody's going to find your name one day.   #warm
cheer: My gran grows prize marrows. Very strict.
  them: Then you come from careful people. Holt would approve.   #funny

== patrol-chats
when: tier>=colleague !who:holt
them: On patrol you get stopped every ten steps. "Is the lift slow?" "Have you seen my mug?"
them: I used to mind. Now it's my favourite bit. You get to know everyone that way.   #warm
ask: What do people ask you most, about your job?
listen: Have you found many mugs?
  them: Seven this month. Four were in the garden. People drink tea with plants, apparently.   #funny
share: "Can you fix this?" Every time.
  them: Ha. The Works curse. Everyone's got a kettle that "makes a noise".   #funny
cheer: Where the toilets are.
  them: A Watch question too. Every deck has them. Follow the signs. You're welcome.   #funny

== watch-office-tea
when: tier>=colleague !who:holt
them: The Watch office kettle's older than me. It's been mended four times. By your lot.
them: It sounds like a small storm. We love it. Holt pretends not to.   #funny
ask: Is there something old aboard you'd hate to see replaced?
listen: Will you ever get a new one?
  them: Over our dead kettle. Sorry. Over its dead element. Same thing.   #funny
share: The old washer on Deck 4.
  them: The loud one? Ha. Every Works tech has a soft spot for that washer.
cheer: Me. I'm vintage now.
  them: You've been here five minutes. Come back in ten years.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- friend: what it means

== switch-off
when: tier>=friend rank:junior
them: On the Watch you think about what could go wrong, all shift. Then you take it to dinner.
them: I check my own bunk ladder before I climb it. Every night. My bunkmates laugh.   #funny
ask: How do you leave the day behind, at the end of it?
listen: Does it ever switch off?
  them: On rest days, by midday. Well. Teatime. Nearly.   #funny
share: A shower, and somebody to talk to.
  them: Somebody to talk to. Yes. That's most of it, I think.   #warm
cheer: I don't. I bring it to dinner.
  them: Then sit with me. We'll worry about doors together.   #warm

== all-present
when: tier>=friend who:mensah|achterberg-lars|garcia-greta|park-noor|castellano-jem
them: End of a night round, I write two words in the log. "All present."
them: Two words. Some nights they're the best two words I know.   #warm
ask: What's the best thing your work lets you say, at the end of the day?
listen: Was there ever a night you couldn't?
  them: Not a real one. A late lift, a lost bunkmate. Found. Always found. That's the Wren.   #warm
share: "It's fixed." I love saying that.
  them: Good words, those. We're in the same business, really. "It's fine now."   #warm
cheer: "All done. Bed."
  them: Two good words as well. Close enough to mine.   #funny

== proud-watch
when: tier>=friend !who:holt|dufresne-cora|tomas
them: My proudest Watch moment? A junior got lost on Deck 2 their first week. Crying, a bit.
them: I walked them back the long way, naming every door. They were laughing by the lift.   #warm
ask: What's a small kindness you're proud of?
listen: Do they still remember?
  them: They say hello every morning. That's how I know.   #warm
share: Helping someone find their way.
  them: Then it got passed on. That's the best a kindness can do.   #warm
cheer: Holding the lift for a stranger.
  them: That's a good one. Small and kind. That's the Wren.   #warm

== what-watch-means
when: tier>=friend !who:holt
them: Can I tell you what the Watch means to me? It means somebody's always awake.
them: Whatever happens, at any hour, there's a face in the Watch office. Today, it's mine.   #warm
ask: What's the hour you'd least like to give up?
listen: Doesn't that get tiring?
  them: Sometimes. Then I see the bunk rooms dark and quiet, and it's worth it.   #warm
share: The hour before breakfast, when it's quiet.
  them: Same. That's when the ship tells you how she slept.   #warm
cheer: My future self. With a pension.
  them: Ha. Very sensible. Very Watch.   #funny

== watch-habit
when: tier>=friend !who:holt
them: The Watch gave me a habit I can't lose. I count exits in every room. Even the mess.
them: At home on leave, my family thinks I'm planning to run. I'm not. Probably.   #funny
ask: Has your job given you a habit that's followed you home?
listen: How many exits has the mess got?
  them: Three. Four if you count the galley hatch. Brennan says I may not count it.   #funny
share: I listen to every machine I pass.
  them: That's the Works one. We all have one. Nobody's normal by year two.   #funny
cheer: I tidy other people's spanners.
  them: That one's catching. Half of Works has it. One of you started it.   #funny

== night-favourite
when: tier>=friend who:mensah|achterberg-lars|garcia-greta|park-noor|castellano-jem
them: People pity the night Watch. They shouldn't. We get the ship when she's honest.
them: No rush, no queue, just her and us. I wouldn't swap it now.   #warm
ask: What's a time of day that feels like yours?
listen: Do you ever see the sunrise?
  them: No sun out here. But the lights warm up at six. Close enough. I watch it every day.   #warm
share: Early morning, before anyone's up.
  them: Then we'd overlap. Say hello at six. I'll be just finishing.   #warm
cheer: The walk back from the gym.
  them: Fine choice. Quiet corridors, sore legs. Lovely.   #funny

== thursday-checks
when: tier>=friend !rank:junior !who:holt
them: Thursday's bunk inspection. Juniors dread it. I love it, secretly.
them: It's not about tidy. It's a chance to see everyone's all right. A bunk tells you a lot.   #warm
ask: What would your bunk tell someone about you?
listen: What does a bunk tell you?
  them: Who's homesick. Who's sleeping badly. Who's got a new Gerald. All good to know.   #warm
share: That I'm settling in. Bit by bit.
  them: Then it's saying the right thing. I'll be glad to read it.   #warm
cheer: That I fold nothing. Ever.
  them: That says you're busy, not bad. I'll mark you down kindly.   #funny
